# Portable build after every change (mandatory)

The user runs **`dist-portable\llmchat.exe`**. Source edits alone do not update what they use.

**Before the final reply of any change set** (frontend, backend/sidecar, Tauri, CSS, pricing, scripts, etc.):

1. `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\prepare-sidecar.ps1`
2. From `frontend/`: `npm run tauri -- build` (ensure VS/Cargo env as usual)
3. If `dist-portable\llmchat.exe` / `llmchat-backend` is locked, stop those processes, then continue
4. `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\make-portable.ps1`
5. Confirm in the reply: portable ready at `dist-portable\llmchat.exe`

**Do this by default.** Do not skip because the change “looks small”, because the user did not ask, or because a conversation summary omitted packaging. Only skip if the user explicitly says not to package.

If a step fails, report the error; never claim the portable build succeeded.
